/*
 * The Cell PPE instruction set (PowerPC 2.02 Book I + VMX, the subset the PPE implements), as an X-macro:
 *
 *   PS_PPU_OP(id, mnemonic, format, primary, xo, flags)
 *
 * id        Op enumerator (pspocket/ppu/decoder.hpp)
 * mnemonic  base mnemonic; "o" (OE) / "." (Rc) / "l" (LK) / "a" (AA) suffixes are added by the disassembler
 * format    operand format (Fmt), drives decoding, disassembly, register usage and the generic encoder
 * primary   primary opcode (bits 0-5)
 * xo        extended opcode, meaning depends on the group:
 *             19, 31        bits 21-30 (10 bits); XO-forms with OPF_OE also match xo | 0x200 (bit 21 = OE)
 *             30            MD-forms: bits 27-29 (3 bits); MDS-forms: bits 27-30 (4 bits)
 *             58, 62        bits 30-31
 *             59, 63 A-form bits 26-30 (5 bits);  63 X-form: bits 21-30
 *             4 (VMX)       VX: bits 21-31 (11 bits); VXR: bits 22-31 (+ Rc at bit 21); VA: bits 26-31
 * flags     OPF_* (decoder.hpp)
 *
 * The opcode values follow RPCS3's decoder table, rpcs3/Emu/Cell/PPUOpcodes.h (ppu_decoder).
 */

